<title>UK: Brown - 10p income tax rate as soon as prudent.</title>
<headline>Brown - 10p income tax rate as soon as prudent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said in his maiden budget that he would introduce a 10 pence starting rate of income tax as soon as it was prudent to do so.</p>
<p>&quot;We will introduce a 10p rate of income tax as soon as it is prudent to do so,&quot; he told parliament.</p>
<p>The starting rate of income tax is now 20 pence.</p>
<p>&quot;A 10p tax rate, combined with a cut in benefit tapers, will reduce in-work poverty,&quot; Brown said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
